ntable-Implementations"]]},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile/RawRepresentable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[],"title":"RawRepresentable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/rawrepresentable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/RawRepresentable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Which security posture a client is registered under (X5.1). This is the FAPI “one switch”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"FAPI 2.0 is not a single feature but a bundle of constraints — mandatory PAR, mandatory PKCE"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"code":"S256","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mandatory strong client authentication, mandatory sender-constrained tokens,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a refusal of every relaxation the base specs permit. Encoding them as one profile rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a dozen independent booleans means an operator cannot register a client that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nearly"}]},{"type":"text","text":" FAPI, and a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change at all, because "},{"identifier":"Self::Standard","type":"reference","i